{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Blue Eyes Cryin in the Rain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]In the twilight glow I see her
[D]Blue eyes cryin' in the [G]rain
[G]When we kissed good-bye and parted
I [D]knew we'd never meet [G]again
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Love is like a dying ember
[G]Only memories [D7]remain
[G]And through the ages I'll remember
[D7]Blue eyes crying in the [G]rain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Break over Verse
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[C]Someday when we meet up yonder
[G]We'll stroll hand in hand [D7]again
[G]In the land that knows no parting
[D7]Blue eyes crying in the [G]rain.
{end_of_verse}
